p(27,12,"The next day after the farrier had examined my wounds, he said he hoped",
 "The farrier hopes the joint is not hurt. The horse might still work, but would always have a mark. The cure was long and painful.",
 "The next day, after the farrier had looked at my wounds, he said he hoped the joint was not hurt. If it was not, I would not be spoiled for work, but I would always keep the mark. I believe they did their best to make a good cure, but it was a long and painful one. What they called proud flesh came up in my knees and was burned out with a strong chemical. When it was at last healed, they put a liquid on the front of both knees to make all the hair come off. They had some reason for this, and I think it was all right.",
 ["examined","blemish","caustic","blistering fluid"])
